for them to do it. And, you know, I want people to know that they have choices. So it's dialogue with a person who wants to do it face to face, not Facebook to Facebook. So really the idea is that this is a conversation that people are having either in person or it could be on Skype or Zoom or on the phone even, but not in writing and certainly not in social media. And with people who have differing perspectives and those differing perspectives don't have to be the most extreme differences. So that really frames what I want to help people do. And in terms of the difference between that and some of the other kinds of conversations people might have, diatribe or discourse or debate, this is not about trying to win an argument.
让他们去这么做。而且，你知道的，我希望人们知道他们是有选择的。所以，这是与一个想要进行对话的人面对面地交谈，而不是“脸书”对“脸书”（Facebook to Facebook）。因此，真正的理念是，这是一场人们当面进行的对话，也可以通过Skype、Zoom甚至电话进行，但绝不是以文字形式，当然也不是在社交媒体上。并且是与那些有着不同观点的人进行的，而这些不同的观点不必是最极端的差异。这才是真正界定了我想帮助人们做的事情。至于这与其他类型的人们可能会进行的对话（如抨击、交流或辩论）之间的区别，这并不是为了赢得争论。

